{"c":[{"id":"362f7f2441a3fcab","sum":"R3: corpus m36/m43 miss event cards by the producer's rule (relative date, no anchor), m37 finds no person: event-card code, not the router. routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as a caret, since RouteFollower sends none then.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-9c33f255f5c1caad","text":"R3: corpus m36/m43 list no event card by the producer's rule (a conversation line's relative date has no anchor); m37 finds no person. Those misses are event-card code, not the router.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-dcc2d733c48b884a","text":"R3: RouteFollower sends no routingContext while the selection is a plain caret, so routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as caret; comparing them ended every write session at the host's first sentence end.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e516245b6d5f910e","sum":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only with left[] empty; runs.ts owes every required or recipient field in windows a goal writes. A goal value's display names its source window, so goal-prompt.ts says pick values by their quoted part.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-100b242cff553f5d","text":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only when left[] is empty (partial/handoff otherwise); runs.ts owes every field left.ts marks required or recipient in windows a goal writes in, and a closed window leaves them unresolved.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-33695164e4940cad","text":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so live qwen3.8 matched v.display.includes('ORD-...') to the sender's email; goal-prompt.ts now says pick values by their quoted part.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
